 `hideChildrenOfValid`, `root`, `hideRoot`, `multiple`, `enableGoUpperDirector`] properties.\n\nThe extra options that this plugin provides are:\n- `onlyShowDir`:  (Boolean) if true, will only show directory. Default: false.\n- `root`: (String) it is the root of file tree. Default: process.cwd(). \n- `onlyShowValid`: (Boolean) if true, will only show valid files (if `validate` is provided). Default: false.\n- `hideChildrenOfValid`: (Boolean) if true, will hide children of valid directories (if `validate` is provided). Default: false.\n- `transformer`: (Function) a hook function to transform the display of directory or file name.\n- `multiple`: (Boolean) if true, will enable to select multiple files. Default: false.\n- `enableGoUpperDirectory`: (Boolean) Show `..` in inside root dir, and the user can press **space** on it to go upper directory. Default: false.\n\nWhen `multiple` is enabled, `default` should be `string[]` type, otherwise it's `string` type.\n### Typescript Support\n\n> version >= 1.0.16\n\n1. Install `@types/inquirer`\n\n2. Ensure you have registered with `file-tree-selection`\n\n```js\ninquirer.registerPrompt('file-tree-selection', inquirerFileTreeSelection)\n```\n\n3. And you will get type support when you code in IDE\n\n![ts](./example/ts.jpeg)\n\n### Example\n\nESM (version ^2)\n\n```js\nimport inquirer from 'inquirer'\nimport inquirerFileTreeSelection from 'inquirer-file-tree-selection-prompt'\n\ninquirer.registerPrompt('file-tree-selection', inquirerFileTreeSelection)\n\ninquirer\n  .prompt([\n    {\n      type: 'file-tree-selection',\n      name: 'file'\n    }\n  ])\n  .then(answers => {\n    console.log(JSON.stringify(answers))\n  });\n```\n\nCJS (version ^1 and <2)\n\n```js\nconst inquirer = require('inquirer')\nconst inquirerFileTreeSelection = require('inquirer-file-tree-selection-prompt')\n\ninquirer.registerPrompt('file-tree-selection', inquirerFileTreeSelection)\n\ninquirer\n  .prompt([\n    {\n      type: 'file-tree-selection',\n      name: 'file'\n    }\n  ])\n  .then(answers => {\n    console.log(JSON.stringify(answers))\n  });\n```\n\n[More examples](./example/)","readmeFilename":"README.md","gitHead":"b7d06913a72c57b482c1d91fca87d1eec2f5a94a","bugs":{"url":"https://github.com/anc95/inquirer-file-tree-selection/issues"},"homepage":"https://github.com/anc95/inquirer-file-tree-selection#readme","_id":"inquirer-file-tree-selection-prompt@2.0.3-test.0","_nodeVersion":"16.3.0","_npmVersion":"7.15.1","dist":{"integrity":"sha512-Fbi3yU1CFGofAFWL+lLUcZyVxcQsHGuzdrZEsOIFIDA4FW3gJ5ZGPLHN4iTgqWUo+9FeGS2NmGJD46pqRdEsRw==","shasum":"5d5a61b821a12977c1f01f1f5a33d718081a48b9","tarball":"https://registry.npmjs.org/inquirer-file-tree-selection-prompt/-/inquirer-file-tree-selection-prompt-2.0.3-test.0.tgz","fileCount":10,"unpackedSize":24189,"signatures":[{"keyid":"SHA256:jl3bwswu80PjjokCgh0o2w5c2U4LhQAE57gj9cz1kzA","sig":"MEUCIDYEngOpvzngj7Ot4nrfJ1ZHRuDxNycvTQK6o6+5IcVkAiEAw+stefKns7u4W/YEQuuUTJFHaOYVyS5XkC0etqtRt1U="}],"npm-signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\r\nVersion: OpenPGP.js v4.10.10\r\nComment: https://openpgpjs.org\r\n\r\nwsFzBAEBCAAGBQJi7Ni7ACEJED1NWxICdlZqFiEECWMYAoorWMhJKdjhPU1b\r\nEgJ2Vmol8Q//b7u8anfIw8w6vQWlxVyidX8OcsVR/i6rHA7YhAjyoeuzYpni\r\n55ZtsLRDV5BOYK7oMLLtmuypczPpToUVxdVn4DmQXTVUdJx370fXWGLJgTx7\r\n+9Nr1Fhb5suZwZgVHIm+a1M5KmpaHuCH4/kOWxOhRNcDjdgVBvpCtlldWDLE\r\n10jY2ogn2fdAHDmfxIWmRW8xbXg9GFivHPbxlNyNCZoOBnjPsND6Xrc0YB1H\r\n+oKbtGLJpq+r2pc50vATinR/c7AT1nBPGNN2Ke9l6xwv8dMmIXkBEN28KqNc\r\nVWSgCx0qoMFLgJJxnrQVBxBlkK4FREwo8Zll/WyMn6REUEWlF95oZjo7CXui\r\nvtgfZnt/kxE7tHUjY+OU02Gw4eoK3KQbiu8Cc/7xxdMuPVuL2hOh+GEE5K5z\r\npDCjGY69GtxKGkJLpwxkBEGJcud+iyjhEywuRhxh2jqzbxST/UL0cs0ipWNK\r\nEOFftC4vvoc9UWxWk1hdsyEvbvJq9FD4syn6UoOK7m9HJj5MDb3jwm3YeDXe\r\nGNtZSWy+4SM727BZBdF3k1yW+0pMUyWIDl91mGIDT0wGIXCEkJgle0KUknJR\r\n7e2JC+k+7jz0ylBbmLdnMB35oNHenxUgnHDxBL4bTgC7OkSIeg55dG0/z5CV\r\nWg7GsD1q4asZs+V/O2oWoCD004YFDzobJUY=\r\n=L75w\r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\r\n"},"_npmUser":{"name":"anc95","email":"148